84
00:04:19,440 --> 00:04:22,700
I like to have many choices to choose from.

85
00:04:22,700 --> 00:04:26,440
So variety means something that has many options.

86
00:04:26,440 --> 00:04:30,600
For example, at the grocery store, there's a great variety of food.

87
00:04:30,600 --> 00:04:34,280
There are apples and crackers and cakes and wine.

88
00:04:34,280 --> 00:04:37,080
So variety means there are many different kinds of something.

89
00:04:37,100 --> 00:04:37,320
Okay.

90
00:04:37,500 --> 00:04:38,120
So many choices.

91
00:04:39,080 --> 00:04:44,240
At the bookstore, you can find a variety of books and magazines, for example.

92
00:04:44,240 --> 00:04:45,240
All right.

93
00:04:45,240 --> 00:04:56,600
Now moving on to, again, when we're talking about the period of time, how often she's going to get this cooking magazine, the one that he's showing her is a bi-monthly publication.

94
00:04:57,840 --> 00:05:01,920
So what exactly does it mean if she receives a magazine bi-monthly?

95
00:05:01,920 --> 00:05:02,920
Okay.

96
00:05:03,250 --> 00:05:05,230
So this is a bit confusing in English.

97
00:05:05,960 --> 00:05:12,760
Bi-monthly has two meanings, but what's important is the word bi- here or the prefix bi-.

98
00:05:12,760 --> 00:05:13,350
That means two.

99
00:05:13,760 --> 00:05:14,760
Okay.

100
00:05:14,760 --> 00:05:15,760
Okay.

101
00:05:15,760 --> 00:05:19,360
So we could say bi-monthly, bi-weekly, bi-annually.

102
00:05:19,360 --> 00:05:19,910
These all mean two.

103
00:05:20,640 --> 00:05:25,090
So in this case, we're talking about something that I receive two times every month.

104
00:05:25,450 --> 00:05:25,730
Okay.

105
00:05:26,680 --> 00:05:31,440
Or it can be that you get it once every two months.

106
00:05:31,440 --> 00:05:31,740
Okay.

107
00:05:32,440 --> 00:05:32,940
So that might be confusing.

108
00:05:33,440 --> 00:05:34,440
Right.

109
00:05:34,440 --> 00:05:40,560
So let's just say that it's the month of October and I have this great subscription to a magazine.

110
00:05:40,580 --> 00:05:43,100
So in October, I will receive it two times.

111
00:05:43,480 --> 00:05:43,780
Exactly.

112
00:05:44,400 --> 00:05:46,000
So you get it twice.

113
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:55,890
Or it could also mean that you receive the magazine in October and then you don't receive another magazine until December.

114
00:05:56,290 --> 00:05:58,050
So it's a bi-monthly publication.

115
00:05:58,640 --> 00:06:00,240
Every other month.

116
00:06:00,240 --> 00:06:00,630
Every two months.

117
00:06:01,240 --> 00:06:02,240
Right.

118
00:06:02,240 --> 00:06:03,240
So this is very confusing for us.

119
00:06:03,240 --> 00:06:11,090
It's confusing for you, but if you see this word bi-monthly or bi-weekly, you should ask the person who's offering the subscription what kind they mean.

120
00:06:11,360 --> 00:06:14,630
Is it every month two times or is it every other month?

121
00:06:15,350 --> 00:06:15,910
All right.

122
00:06:16,080 --> 00:06:16,710
So exactly.

123
00:06:17,200 --> 00:06:19,690
Just remember the prefix bi- means two.

124
00:06:20,280 --> 00:06:28,620
And then if it's bi-monthly, bi-annual, bi-weekly, you have to more or less make sure that they specify what they mean because it can mean both.

125
00:06:28,840 --> 00:06:30,500
And that's how ambiguous this word is.

126
00:06:30,640 --> 00:06:31,640
It is.

127
00:06:31,640 --> 00:06:35,520
So the next one, the next word we have for you is not nearly as confusing.

128
00:06:35,520 --> 00:06:42,940
It's a very, very common word in both periodicals and sales, but also in marketing and business as well.

129
00:06:43,600 --> 00:06:44,600
Right.

130
00:06:44,600 --> 00:06:50,240
We're talking about a quarterly publication or something that comes out once every quarter.

131
00:06:50,700 --> 00:06:50,860
Right.

132
00:06:50,860 --> 00:06:53,280
So if you think about a year, a year has 12 months.

133
00:06:53,580 --> 00:06:55,240
A quarter of a year is three months.

134
00:06:56,040 --> 00:06:59,040
So the first quarter is January, February, March.

135
00:06:59,040 --> 00:07:00,040
Exactly.

136
00:07:00,040 --> 00:07:04,680
So a quarterly publication means that you will get a magazine four times in one year.

137
00:07:04,680 --> 00:07:05,680
Okay.

138
00:07:05,680 --> 00:07:07,000
We could also talk about quarterly sales.

139
00:07:07,760 --> 00:07:11,760
You know, this quarter our business did very well, but last quarter was not so good.

140
00:07:11,760 --> 00:07:13,560
So quarter means three months at a time.

141
00:07:13,780 --> 00:07:14,240
Exactly.

142
00:07:14,820 --> 00:07:20,320
And for our last word on language takeaway today, we are talking about a weekly newsletter.

143
00:07:20,820 --> 00:07:22,340
So weekly is pretty straightforward.

144
00:07:22,680 --> 00:07:24,200
You receive it once every week.

145
00:07:24,200 --> 00:07:24,380
That's right.

146
00:07:25,200 --> 00:07:27,700
So weekly publications are very common.

147
00:07:27,700 --> 00:07:28,520
What is a newsletter?

148
00:07:29,020 --> 00:07:34,340
A newsletter is important in periodicals because it's not a magazine, but it's not a letter either.

149
00:07:34,720 --> 00:07:47,580
It's basically a short update, a couple of pages maybe, or even one page that's on a piece of paper that gives you information about a group or a club or a community.

150
00:07:48,080 --> 00:07:52,540
For example, we could say the EnglishPod newsletter comes out quarterly.

151
00:07:53,100 --> 00:07:53,340
Exactly.

152
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:57,360
Maybe in your offices you receive your company's newsletter.

153
00:07:57,680 --> 00:08:14,020
So usually some companies will come out with a monthly or a quarterly newsletter where if you have many offices or many branches all over the country or the world, then you will receive updates or news about what's going on in other places within your same company.

154
00:08:15,040 --> 00:08:16,040
That's right.

155
00:08:16,040 --> 00:08:18,800
So these are very useful for communication across the company.

156
00:08:18,800 --> 00:08:26,600
You can tell some people in your New York office that in Los Angeles we have a new cafeteria or a new employee.

157
00:08:27,240 --> 00:08:27,400
Exactly.

158
00:08:28,240 --> 00:08:30,620
So that is what a newsletter is basically for.

159
