00:09:48,680 --> 00:09:48,970
Fluency Builder.

181
00:09:49,680 --> 00:10:00,170
Okay, this first phrase is very, very common among sales and sales people because basically it's a way to be polite and to ask someone to listen to you for a little while.

182
00:10:01,440 --> 00:10:05,030
The salesperson says, if you could spare five minutes of your time.

183
00:10:05,680 --> 00:10:07,970
Okay, so let's start with that part.

184
00:10:08,240 --> 00:10:09,090
If you could spare.

185
00:10:09,730 --> 00:10:13,850
So to spare something means do you have something extra?

186
00:10:14,410 --> 00:10:15,830
Do you have enough of it?

187
00:10:16,180 --> 00:10:19,900
Yeah, so I could say, can you spare $5?

188
00:10:20,460 --> 00:10:21,720
I forgot my wallet at home.

189
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:24,280
So that means do you have an extra $5 I could borrow?

190
00:10:24,720 --> 00:10:25,560
Okay, very good.

191
00:10:25,960 --> 00:10:33,100
So if you're asking someone to spare five minutes of their time, you're asking them to give you five minutes of their time.

192
00:10:33,340 --> 00:10:33,820
That's right.

193
00:10:34,200 --> 00:10:39,120
So if you could spare a second or if you could spare five minutes of your time, I would like to talk to you.

194
00:10:39,280 --> 00:10:42,460
Okay, so it's a very polite way to ask someone for their time.

195
00:10:42,760 --> 00:10:47,020
Now for our next phrase, the woman is also very polite.

196
00:10:47,200 --> 00:10:48,200
She says, you know what?

197
00:10:48,200 --> 00:10:49,200
I have to walk the dog.

198
00:10:49,200 --> 00:10:50,760
